---
const points = [
  {
    title: 'A shelf you can query',
    body: 'One list of what the household actually has — quantity, unit, where it lives — editable in seconds and readable at a glance on your own phone.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Warnings you can act on',
    body: 'Low stock and expiry are shown as days and units, with the reason beside them. Reminders arrive as one short summary of what goes off soon, not one alert per item.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A shopping list with a memory',
    body: 'Things you run out of land on the list because they ran out. HomeMind estimates when you will need something next from how fast you used the last few, and says so.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Scan instead of type',
    body: 'Point the camera at a barcode and the name fills itself in, from the open Open Food Facts database. Typing still works for everything; the camera only saves time.',
  },
  {
    title: 'One household, several phones',
    body: 'Invite the people you live with with a code that works once, for two days. Everyone sees the same items, stock and shopping list, and anyone can leave.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Works without a signal',
    body: 'The phone holds the working copy, so the app works in a basement shop. Changes sync when you are back online, retry on their own, and say so when two phones edited the same thing.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="purpose" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
  <div class="shell stack">
    <header class="section__head">
      <p class="t-overline">What it is for</p>
      <h2 class="t-title" id="purpose-title">Household inventory, minus the guilt</h2>
      <p class="t-lead measure">
        HomeMind is aimed at one specific annoyance: buying something you already have three of, and
        discovering the fourth one the week after it expired. It keeps a plain record and does the
        small arithmetic on top of it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid">
      {
        points.map((point) => (
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="t-card-title">{point.title}</h3>
            <p class="t-secondary">{point.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="t-caption measure">
      All six are built and tested, but none has shipped: there is no public release yet. The
      honest status is in <a href="#status">Where the build stands</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
